    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="0629" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.1216M/148.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3,
                        1910</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Engineer J. A. Ockerson, of the Interior Department, has been appointed by the
                    President as commissioner to cooperate with the commissioner appointed by the
                    Mexican Government to examine the conditions along the Colorado River and to
                    consider the construction of the proposed protective levee. Information as to
                    time and place of meeting will be sent later.</p>
                <p>A satisfactory plan has been presented to the Department by the Mexican
                    ambassador. Express appreciation and gratification to the Mexican Government for
                    the prompt consideration given to this matter, and say that a clause is desired
                    in the agreement specifying free entry of subsistence, supplies, tools,
                    equipment, appliances, and <pb facs="0630" n="548" xml:id="pg548"/> material for
                    the construction of the levee, it being understood that any material remaining
                    unconsumed when the work is completed will be reimported into the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
